# Shang-Chi, Master of Kung Fu: "You may activate abilities of creatures you control as though those creatures had haste"
# (CR 302.6) and "{T}: Add two mana of any one color. Spend this mana only to activate abilities of creature sources" (CR
# 106.6, 602.2b). Turn 1 Bot1 casts Shang-Chi, Basking Rootwalla and Llanowar Elves (Forest and Black Lotus). Shang-Chi
# taps for {G}{G} the turn it arrived, itself one of the creatures; that mana and the Elves' {G} would be three, yet Bramble
# Familiar ({1}{G}) from the hand is not offered: only the Elves' {G} may pay a spell. The {G}{G} pays the Rootwalla's
# "{1}{G}: +2/+2" (an ability of a creature source): it is a 3/3. The Elves, just cast, tap for {G}. Nothing has haste:
# the creatures are still summoning sick (CR 302.6), so none may attack (the declare attackers step asks nothing). Turn 2 Bot2's own Llanowar Elves, cast that turn, can't tap: Shang-Chi is Bot1's, "creatures
# you control".

